1
00:00:00,233 --> 00:00:01,667
The rice is cut.

2
00:00:01,867 --> 00:00:03,033
The clock starts.

3
00:00:03,367 --> 00:00:04,300
In north India,

4
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:05,600
farmers have only a few

5
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:06,667
weeks between the paddy

6
00:00:06,667 --> 00:00:08,267
harvest and sowing wheat.

7
00:00:08,367 --> 00:00:10,167
The field has to be cleared.

8
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:10,867
And the straw

9
00:00:10,867 --> 00:00:12,533
left behind is bulky,

10
00:00:12,900 --> 00:00:13,100
loose,

11
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:14,833
and slow to move.

12
00:00:14,967 --> 00:00:15,867
Without a baler,

13
00:00:15,867 --> 00:00:16,233
a buyer,

14
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:17,200
or a truck,

15
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:19,500
the fastest option is a matchstick.

16
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:20,600
That is why the smoke

17
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,733
comes back every autumn.

18
00:00:23,800 --> 00:00:24,133
Now,

19
00:00:24,133 --> 00:00:25,600
the same straw,

20
00:00:25,600 --> 00:00:26,967
with a plan.

21
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:28,300
The harvest ends.

22
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:29,367
A baler arrives

23
00:00:29,367 --> 00:00:31,100
and packs the straw.

24
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:32,167
Within days,

25
00:00:32,167 --> 00:00:33,933
an aggregator picks it up.

26
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:34,767
The field is clear

27
00:00:34,767 --> 00:00:36,100
in time for wheat.

28
00:00:36,200 --> 00:00:37,733
The straw becomes pellets.

29
00:00:38,067 --> 00:00:38,767
The pellets go

30
00:00:38,767 --> 00:00:40,933
to a plant that needs them.

31
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,333
Same field.

32
00:00:42,567 --> 00:00:43,733
Same few weeks.

33
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:45,300
A different ending.

34
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:46,800
What decides it is whether

35
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:48,267
the farmer can find a baler

36
00:00:48,267 --> 00:00:50,633
and a buyer in time.

37
00:00:51,033 --> 00:00:53,333
IndiaBiomass is building that connection.
